id: E1001-draft-2301_80739235
trigger_tool: conan|cmake|target-runner
phase: target_validation|testing
error_signature: "DB->put: method not permitted before handle's open method|HARMONY_TEST_PASS=1/1"
severity: 2
category: api-lifecycle|ohos|testing|conan
match_keywords: database handle lifecycle, explicit open before CRUD, target consumer probe, temporary database cleanup
title: C API target probes must exercise the required handle lifecycle before CRUD calls
root_cause: A target probe called a Berkeley DB handle's put method immediately after db_create, but Berkeley DB requires the handle to be opened with a database type and path before any CRUD operation. The host consumer passed because it used the complete open-put-get-close lifecycle, while the HarmonyOS-specific probe bypassed that contract and failed at runtime.
affected_scope: C/C++ Conan consumer tests and HarmonyOS target probes for libraries whose factory-created handles require an explicit open or initialize phase before read/write operations.
verification_cmd: "compile the probe against the frozen package; execute it with the package runtime closure; require HARMONY_TEST_PASS=1/1 and verify the temporary database path is absent after exit"
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: lifecycle-complete-target-probe
rec_description: Model the target probe on the library's documented state machine: create, configure/open, perform the minimal operation, close, and remove task-local artifacts on every exit path. Keep the probe independent from host-only behavior and bind it to the exact package include/library tree.
rec_command: "cc -I<package>/include <probe.c> -L<package>/lib -Wl,-rpath,<package>/lib -l<library> -o <probe>; <probe>"
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: manual
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: consumer-first-contract
fallback_description: Reuse the upstream consumer's complete lifecycle as the minimum target assertion, then add only platform-specific path or signer checks required by the target. Never interpret successful factory creation as proof that the handle is ready for CRUD.
fallback_command: "run the existing consumer and target probe separately; record each RC and output"
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: manual
forbid_1_pattern: "db_create.*put.*without.*open"
forbid_1_reason: The factory may return a valid handle whose methods reject operations until the explicit initialization or open phase completes.
forbid_1_consequence: Target validation fails at runtime with a lifecycle error even though compilation and package linking succeed.
forbid_2_pattern: "ignore target probe failure|mark HARMONY_TEST_PASS without execution"
forbid_2_reason: A target-specific test is a Pre-PR and W3 input; replacing its execution with a static or host-only result removes evidence of target behavior.
forbid_2_consequence: The package can be submitted without proving the advertised HarmonyOS API path.
principles: P003, P007, P018
